## Don't do by hand what `crate` does exactly

Mechanics have commands, and they cost nothing to run:

| | |
|---|---|
| `crate capture` | pull sessions into `raw/` |
| `crate pending` | which raw sources aren't in the wiki yet |
| `crate new <type> "<Title>"` | scaffold a page, frontmatter filled in |
| `crate fmt` | put every page's paragraphs back on one line each |
| `crate index` | regenerate `index.md` from every page's `summary:` |
| `crate log <op> --title` | append one entry to `log.md` |
| `crate lint` | dead wikilinks, orphans, missing index entries |

Run these from the vault root; they all take `--vault .`.

Ask me to add a command before you hand-roll a mechanical job.

## Operations

- `/ingest` — fold new raw sources into the wiki. **Discuss the takeaways with me first.** That
  step isn't optional; without it you're a summarizer.
- `/ask` — answer from the wiki. Read `index.md` first, then only the pages it points at. An answer
  worth keeping gets promoted to `wiki/syntheses/`, indexed, and logged.
- `/lint` — contradictions, stale claims, concepts referenced with no page.
